   Getafe, Madrid},
Journal = {CIUDAD Y TERRITORIO-ESTUDIOS TERRITORIALES-CYTET},
Year = {2026},
Volume = {58},
Number = {228},
Pages = {966-977},
Month = {SUM},
Abstract = {Industrial estates have significant health impacts due to the
   concentration of pollutants affecting both workers and surrounding
   neighbourhoods. This paper presents an academic experience developed
   within the Master's Degree in Urban and Territorial Planning (UPM),
   focused on the design of a Health Action Plan for the industrial estates
   of Los Olivos and Los \& Aacute;ngeles in Getafe (Madrid). Based on a
   diagnostic approach grounded in the Guide for Planning Healthy Cities,
   various deficits are identified, related to key urban issues such as
   mobility, green infrastructure, and functional complexity. The proposal
   includes strategies for walkability, urban nature, and social
   interaction, together with an innovative ordinance aimed at fostering
   healthier industrial environment.},
